From: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
Subject: media: camss: add SM8150 (Xiaomi Redmi K20 Pro) support

SM8150 uses the CAMSS 480 / CSIPHY 3 nm block with four CSIPHYs, two CSIDs
plus two CSID-lite, two VFE480 plus two VFE-lite, and the TITAN_TOP GDSC in
CAMCC.  The GIC interrupt assignments match SM8250 for the first four CSIPHYs
and for both CSIDs/VFEs (verified against the stock Android device tree of
this device), and the register bases are:

  CSIPHY0-3  0xac65000 0xac66000 0xac67000 0xac68000
  CSID0/1    0xacb3000 0xacba000    CSID-lite0/1 0xacc8000 0xaccf000
  VFE0/1     0xacaf000 0xacb6000    VFE-lite0/1  0xacc4000 0xaccb000

The board device tree cannot reference the CAMCC clock controller by phandle:
that node carries no phandle and adding one to a live tree through an overlay
crashes the property-change notifier chain (of_property_notify).  Resolve the
CAMSS clocks by node path instead, and make the CAMSS power domains optional so
the driver can probe on a board DT that cannot describe them.

Build-tested on 7.3.0-rc5-sm8150-gc033da1fc4fe (clang + ThinLTO kernel, module
built out of tree with gcc against the installed headers).

Signed-off-by: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
Reviewed-by: (pending hardware validation)
